The first consideration in this strategy is where the product is take-back form user or collect from manufacturers. In the second sample predict how to take-back the product can be easier. Designer should considerate for this strategy

- Timing of take-back (during the take-back process takes places,  technological components can get obsolete);
- Develop different strategies for different take-back programs (B2C, B2B, SME and Large Enterprise);
- Ecorage users or retailers to give-back products;
- Consider the geographic take-back system and reselling;
- Consider where, when and from whom the product should get back in the system in the next loops;
- Consider the return flow of the products and design the next production according to it;
- Take into consideration if your porduct is long-lasting, seasonal or short lifecycle
products;